The water for the potatoes is boiling.
I look at my phone again.
The chef in the video claps his hands.
"Now we make the Bouletten!" he calls out cheerfully.
"First, take half a kilo of minced meat."
"Then mix the meat with an egg and the diced onions."
"Add a soaked Brötchen and two tablespoons of mustard."
I dice the onions and soak the Brötchen in water.
I do exactly what the chef says.
I put the meat, the egg and the onions into a large bowl.
Then I add the Brötchen and the mustard.
"After that, knead everything well with your hands!" he says loudly.
I smile and roll up my sleeves.
My hands get completely messy.
But it is really a lot of fun.
Finally, I form flat, round patties.
They already look very authentic.
Lena and Timo will definitely be happy about the meal!
